# Performance Checklist

- Choose data structures and algorithms suited for expected scale.
- Minimize allocations and redundant data fetches.
- Prefer batched reads and avoid N+1 query patterns.
- Use non-blocking I/O for external calls where practical.
- Apply caching only for clearly expensive or frequently repeated work.

## Before Finishing

- Hot paths avoid unnecessary object creation.
- External calls are bounded with timeouts/retries where needed.
- Any cache has clear invalidation/TTL behavior.
